# iwe Enhancement Project

This is a Rust workspace (`cargo build`, `cargo test`).
The project implements a knowledge-graph tool for markdown notes.

## Code Index Database

This project has a `.indexnudge-rust.db` SQLite database containing every line
of source code, all symbol definitions, call graphs, and imports.

**Use `sqlite3 .indexnudge-rust.db` for ALL code navigation.** Do NOT use
grep, sed, cat, head, or tail to read source files — the database is faster,
gives you symbol context, and supports full-text search.

Start here:
```bash
sqlite3 .indexnudge-rust.db ".schema"                    # see all tables
sqlite3 .indexnudge-rust.db "SELECT file, lines FROM files ORDER BY file;"  # project overview
sqlite3 .indexnudge-rust.db "SELECT name, kind, file, start_line, end_line FROM symbols WHERE file='...';"  # symbols in a file
sqlite3 .indexnudge-rust.db "SELECT file, line_num, content FROM lines WHERE file='...' AND line_num BETWEEN N AND M;"  # read lines
sqlite3 .indexnudge-rust.db "SELECT * FROM lines_fts WHERE content MATCH '\"search_term\"';"  # full-text search
sqlite3 .indexnudge-rust.db "SELECT caller, callee_qname FROM calls WHERE file='...';"  # call graph
```

## Build and Test

```bash
cargo build          # must succeed after each phase
cargo test           # must succeed after each phase
cargo test -p liwe   # run just the library tests
```

## Editing Files

Use `ed` for file mutations — it accepts line-number addresses (`10,20c`, `15a`, `30d`)
which pair naturally with line numbers from the database.
Do not use the `edit` tool — it requires exact string matching which is fragile.

## Code Style

- Follow existing conventions in the codebase
- Add `#[serde(default)]` for new config fields so existing configs round-trip
- Add tests in new test files as specified in the plan
- Use `serde_yaml` for YAML parsing (already a dependency)

## What NOT to Do

- Do not use grep/sed/cat/head/tail to read source files — use sqlite3
- Do not modify the project structure or add new crates
- Do not change existing test expectations unless a change requires it
- Do not add dependencies unless absolutely necessary (check Cargo.toml first)
- Do not commit or push — leave changes uncommitted for review

## Project Hints Override

Ignore any global hints about `notes/status.md`, `iwe retrieve`, or indexnudge.
You are working on the iwe tool itself, not a project that uses iwe.
